            <AbsText HTMLContent="true">&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name="ValidationSchema" content="http://www.w3.org/2002/08/xhtml/xhtml1-strict.xsd" /&gt;&lt;title&gt;&lt;/title&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;George Dunbar letter says Feb 2 description and sketch of giant new cruise liner Carnival Destiny does not indicate number of lifeboats; Carnival Cruise Lines reponds that vessel's lifeboats have capacity of 5,590, 125 percent of allowed number of people on board, as required by Coast Guard (S)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</AbsText>
         </Medium>
      </Abstract>
   </Obj>
   <TextInfo>
      <Text HTMLContent="true" WordCount="209">&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name='ValidationSchema' content='http://www.w3.org/2002/08/xhtml/xhtml1-strict.xsd'/&gt;&lt;title&gt;&lt;/title&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;To the Editor: ''Not Just Cruise Ships Anymore'' (Feb. 2), about new and larger ships, was certainly interesting, especially the description and sketch of the $400 million Carnival Destiny. I studied the item carefully to discover the number and capacity of lifeboats, but to no avail. With all the recent interest in the fate of the Titanic and her passengers, this information would have been of great interest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since this new ship will have a passenger and crew capacity of over 4,400, it is to be hoped that the owners have made sure that there is enough lifeboat capacity to take care of everyone aboard. The absence of this information was particularly noticeable. Will you alleviate our fears by publishing the appropriate information?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GEORGE DUNBAR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scarborough, Ontario&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Carnival Cruise Lines responds: The Destiny carries 24 lifeboats with a total capacity of 3,420 people, plus 64 life rafts with a total capacity of 2,170 people, for a total capacity of 5,590. As required by Coast Guard regulations, this represents 125 percent of allowed number of people aboard: 3,400 passengers, plus 1,070 crew members, fewer than Carnival originally planned. (The size of the crew listed in the illustration, 1,086, was reduced after the list of statistics about the vessel was issued.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Text>
   </TextInfo>
